# The adversarial-loop ledger is an append-only log: every cycle adds an entry
# at the end, and no two cycles touch each other's text. Git's default merge
# still treats two appends at the same location as a conflict, so with
# branch protection set to strict (a branch must be current with main before
# it merges), EVERY merged cycle PR forced a rebase and a full CI round on
# every other open one -- a dozen of them in a single afternoon, on changes
# that never overlapped in code.
#
# `merge=union` keeps both sides instead of conflicting. For an append-only
# log that is exactly right: each entry is self-labelled with its cycle
# number, so ordering within the tail does not carry meaning.
#
# The one thing to know: union keeps BOTH versions of any line that two
# branches EDIT differently, rather than choosing. Editing existing entries
# from a branch can therefore leave a duplicated line. Edit the ledger on
# main, and let branches only append.
docs/ADVERSARIAL_LOOP_LEDGER.md merge=union
